      "id": "forest",
      "title": "Forest height",
      "description": "Mean height of the forest canopy measured by NASA's GEDI laser instrument on the International Space Station, April 2019 to July 2025 (GEDI L3 Version 3). Fixed scale: 0 m is the bottom and 50 m or more is the top. Where GEDI has no measurement (mostly beyond about 52° N and S) the value comes from the NASA SVS 4950 visualization instead; the two are never blended. Taller forest sounds as a higher, fuller note. This is the fixed base layer.",
